# Parallel-drain merge friction control (CLAUDE.md §7).
#
# These release-plumbing / generated files are the ones multiple
# in-flight branches would otherwise collide on. `union` keeps both
# sides' added lines for append-style files so independent branches
# merge without a hard conflict; `.mo` is a CI-recompiled binary and
# must never be text-merged.
#
# Pair this with: git config rerere.enabled true  (replays known
# conflict resolutions, e.g. the version line).

CHANGES.md        merge=union
readme.txt        merge=union
SEQUENCE.md       merge=union
languages/*.mo    binary

# `languages/*.po merge=union` was here and is deliberately gone (#3864).
#
# A .po is not append-only, which is the only case union is safe for: the
# catalogue regeneration RELOCATES entries, so union kept the appended copy
# and the relocated one, produced a duplicate msgid that msgfmt refuses, and
# reported no conflict while doing it — both copies were "correct".
#
# It did not even buy the conflict reduction it was added for: branches that
# `git merge-tree` resolved cleanly locally were still reported CONFLICTING
# by GitHub on the .po, because the driver runs on a developer's machine and
# not on the server-side merge that actually gates a PR.
#
# A PR now drops languages/pending/<issue>-<slug>.po instead of editing the
# catalogue, so there is nothing left to union. See languages/pending/README.md.

# Report docs are append-heavy (each report change adds its own section),
# so parallel report branches collide on them the same way the release
# plumbing does. Union keeps every branch's added section. Safe: these are
# additive prose docs, never code.
docs/reports.md       merge=union
docs/nl_NL/reports.md merge=union

# Same reasoning for the alerts docs (#2629): each wave of the epic appends
# its own section — preferences, inline surfaces, digests, the catalogue —
# and several of those waves are built on parallel branches. Union keeps
# every branch's added section instead of a hard conflict on prose.
docs/alerts.md        merge=union
docs/nl_NL/alerts.md  merge=union

# Note: never put CODE files under merge=union — it would keep both
# versions of a conflicting line and silently break the code. union is
# only safe for append-only text. The version constant lives in
# talenttrack.php (NOT unioned) and is owned solely by the release step.
docs/comms.md        merge=union
docs/nl_NL/comms.md  merge=union
